*> Convergence harness (test infrastructure, excluded from coverage; plan "Execution mode",
*> Convergence): runs client instances (client/copy/CLSTATE.cpy, each allocated) against one core in
*> this process, frame by frame, either through the client's single-player host (a client's SP-OPEN;
*> further clients attached over additional memory connections of the same core, or over loopback
*> TCP once the world is opened to others) or through the server program's loop (SV-START,
*> SV-ITERATE) on a loopback port. The record is CONVH.cpy.
*>
*>   CV-INIT USING CONVH, directory (PIC X(64), "build/<name>": two levels below the repository
*>     root), length: the directory emptied and created; no clients; the clock at 1000000 ms.
*>   CV-CLIENT-ADD USING CONVH, name (PIC X(16)), name length, index out: a new started client
*>     (CL-INIT, the name, game directory <dir>/<name>, CL-START) on the title screen; its
*>     single-player settings have view distance 2 and no hostile mobs (quicker joins; the rest are
*>     SP-DEFAULTS; a test may change SP-SETTINGS before CV-HOST-OPEN).
*>   CV-HOST-OPEN USING CONVH, index, folder (PIC X(80)), folder length, game mode: that client
*>     opens (or creates) the single-player world saves/<folder> named after the folder (SP-OPEN)
*>     and hosts it: its frames run the core.
*>   CV-ATTACH USING CONVH, index: that client joins the hosted core over a further memory
*>     connection (connecting screen, NET-OPEN-MEMORY), as the host's own client does.
*>   CV-SERVER-START USING CONVH, configuration (PIC X(1024), "|" separates lines; "port=<free
*>     port>" is put first): <dir>/server/cobolcraft-server.conf written, then SV-START in
*>     <dir>/server; CV-PORT is the port. Each frame then runs one server loop iteration with one
*>     core tick before the clients.
*>   CV-SERVER-CONSOLE USING CONVH, line (PIC X(256), the command text, trailing spaces dropped):
*>     the line as typed at the server console (CORE-CONSOLE in <dir>/server); the replies are
*>     printed with the next frame.
*>   CV-SERVER-STOP USING CONVH: the shutdown command at the console, frames until the core has stopped,
*>     SV-SHUTDOWN; the server no longer runs.
*>   CV-JOIN USING CONVH, index, port: the client adds the server-list entry "Convergence" with
*>     address 127.0.0.1:<port>, selects it and clicks Join (three frames).
*>   CV-STEP USING CONVH: one frame 50 ms after the last: the server iteration (when running), then
*>     every client's CL-STEP with its queued events, in client order.
*>   CV-STEPS USING CONVH, count: that many frames.
*>   CV-UNTIL-PLAY USING CONVH, index, joined out: frames (at most 400) until that client is in play
*>     with the player loaded (an earlier PL-LOADED cleared first); joined 1 when it is.
*>   CV-UNTIL-SCREEN USING CONVH, index, screen, reached out: frames (at most 400) until that client
*>     shows that screen.
*>   CV-QUEUE USING CONVH, index, kind, a, x, y (FLOAT-SHORT): queues one input event (shim-abi §8)
*>     for that client's next frame.
*>   CV-KEY USING CONVH, index, key: one frame with that key down and up.
*>   CV-KEY-SET USING CONVH, index, key, kind (CC-EV-KEY-DOWN or CC-EV-KEY-UP): one frame with that
*>     key event (a key held over several frames).
*>   CV-BUTTON-SET USING CONVH, index, button, kind (CC-EV-BUTTON-DOWN or -UP): one frame with that
*>     mouse button event at the window centre.
*>   CV-CLICK USING CONVH, index, action, argument (0 = any), found out: clicks the centre of the
*>     first widget of the client's screen model with that action, in one frame.
*>   CV-TYPE USING CONVH, index, text (PIC X(64)), length: a text event per byte, at most 30 a
*>     frame (the client takes at most 32 typed code points a frame).
*>   CV-SAY USING CONVH, index, text (PIC X(64)), length: chat opened (T), the text typed, Enter:
*>     three frames (a text starting "/" is a command).
*>   CV-TEXTS USING CONVH, index, text out (PIC X(1024)): the texts of the client's current screen
*>     model widgets, "|"-separated.
*>   CV-CHAT-LOG USING CONVH, index, text out (PIC X(4096)): every chat message the client received
*>     this session, oldest first, "|"-separated.
*>   CV-FREE-PORT USING port out: a free loopback port (bound and released).

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. CV-INIT.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-COMMAND             PIC X(160).
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CONVH.
 01 L-DIR                  PIC X(64).
 01 L-LENGTH               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CONVH L-DIR L-LENGTH.
     INITIALIZE CONVH
     MOVE L-DIR TO CV-DIR
     MOVE L-LENGTH TO CV-DIR-LENGTH
     MOVE 1000000 TO CV-NOW
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-COMMAND
     STRING "rm -rf " L-DIR(1:L-LENGTH) " && mkdir -p " L-DIR(1:L-LENGTH) "/server"
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-COMMAND
     CALL "SYSTEM" USING WS-COMMAND
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM CV-INIT.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. CV-CLIENT-ADD.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY COREAPI.
 01 WS-SIZE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PTR                 USAGE POINTER.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CONVH.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-NAME                 PIC X(16).
 01 L-LENGTH               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-INDEX                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CONVH L-NAME L-LENGTH L-INDEX.
     ADD 1 TO CV-COUNT
     MOVE CV-COUNT TO L-INDEX
     MOVE LENGTH OF CLIENT-STATE TO WS-SIZE
     ALLOCATE WS-SIZE CHARACTERS RETURNING WS-PTR
     SET CV-ADDR(L-INDEX) TO WS-PTR
     SET ADDRESS OF CLIENT-STATE TO WS-PTR
     MOVE 0 TO CV-EVENT-COUNT(L-INDEX)
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE L-NAME TO CL-NAME
     MOVE L-LENGTH TO CL-NAME-LENGTH
     MOVE SPACES TO CL-GAME-DIR
     STRING CV-DIR(1:CV-DIR-LENGTH) "/" L-NAME(1:L-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO CL-GAME-DIR
     COMPUTE CL-GAME-DIR-LENGTH = CV-DIR-LENGTH + 1 + L-LENGTH
     CALL "CL-START" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE SP-SETTINGS TO CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE 2 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     MOVE 0 TO CS-HOSTILE-MOBS
     MOVE CORE-SETTINGS TO SP-SETTINGS
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM CV-CLIENT-ADD.

